  "title": "Division with Remainders",
  "level": "primary-2",
  "category": "Arithmetic",
  "introduction": "Build on Primary 1 knowledge and practise division with remainders.",
  "definition": "Sometimes equal grouping leaves some objects unused. The remainder is the amount left after making as many complete groups as possible. It must be less than the positive divisor.",
